<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Schools crisis in France: Investment fails to inspire confidence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca73b3a6d3b8f70420305ac508cf2f41962162fb53f58e02953cca9478406e2</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T19:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/schools-crisis-in-france-investment-fails-to-inspire-confidence/a-79621916--f1c3b3d7b3e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/schools-crisis-in-france-investment-fails-to-inspire-confidence/a-79621916?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For weeks, schoolchildren in France have been protesting the failing education system. Compared to many other countries, France invests heavily in education but critics say that the funds are not distributed fairly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Macron and Steinmeier struggle to revive Franco-German ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:605ebb6346b02038993f142908191e2a8e3d5e50afaff37b8d6515b9753f67b3</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635--64b747b714b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Presidents Frank-Walter Steinmeier and Emmanuel Macron are about to step down from their offices. Their meeting in France made it clear how urgently the Franco-German partnership needs new momentum.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Lifeline for Ukrainian refugees confronts donor fatigue and online abuse as anti-Ukrainian sentiment grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0d6687eaf2f36f91f8377b18501c4e1bdcb2f6aed7e6a58c4599149318891ab</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-se/a-79613292--19cba8c4d4f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-sentiment-grows/a-79613292?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian woman who fled the war in her country built a lifeline for refugees in Poland. Now her organization faces donor fatigue, funding cuts and rising hostility as support for Ukrainians in Poland wanes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia and Herzegovina will soon have a new Grand Mufti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8fcc77adc4ea78b7d806146ae8919d286bed457ce9a447c22389a374c1c25fd</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-will-soon-have-a-new-grand-mufti/a-79604402--960d4eb80e56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-will-soon-have-a-new-grand-mufti/a-79604402?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new leader of the Islamic Community in Bosnia and Herzegovina will be elected on October 10. The reis-ul-ulema's role is not only important for Muslims in the country itself, but could inspire Muslims across Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15f5cbbd733e1e25b503a69f05baf934d50a12682b7536f0c25d71d311e1ef20</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU pulls sponsorship from Disinfo2026 event in Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a4dfd2a0fe958f34fa692e291885863af8c354bb72821304f814cf3fe6b6b6</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615--b060dac4b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's diplomatic service, Canada and host nation Lithuania all pulled support from a disinformation event in Vilnius. Amid reports of US pressure, the EU said it was "uncomfortable with the framing" of some panels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Security in the Black Sea region: is Bulgaria the weak link in Europe's defense against threats from Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbee76b7b85358d49d2cded64909c5ad1ca0bf532e19774dcf355a42a5642388</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-/a-79592663--cd93d129d2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-russia/a-79592663?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two ships have sunk off the coast of Bulgaria and Romania after drone attacks in recent days. Bulgaria has held back on pointing the finger at Russia. What does that mean for security in the Black Sea and the region?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0848b1d7b87c55e5c1b5cc5b5d938c25eee238b2cebd2495c01a617370290d4a</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian data centers, could Ukraine soon be offline?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b80f86f563a3c4d9a41c5887f8393c25dcdb7857ed9994ccbcab2606d8106527</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503--ed9380350022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia targets Ukraine's data centers more and more, experts say the country's internet system is too robust to shut down entirely. However, services could become more expensive.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Middle Corridor: Can Bulgaria be a safe gateway for Asian imports to the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1fef6254dc311fdbf4b166f913d93bfad2b3a11513e9f96524d2fa9ae08f339</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530--0deecfdaf02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants more trade via the Middle Corridor, which could bring big benefits for Bulgaria. But Tuesday's drone attacks on commercial ships off the Bulgarian coast are a stark reminder of the security risks involved.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cc224716cc7a71a3934aca196bf1247df70a93c8c8637d90476485415569149</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca65614bf042488574e345c9743deb3d0422549a2a8c06b8559f09f6486b936</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:052161c43fed9a2043fc20a2efd73ab27991c155600acc1d4956486d286d1a6d</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:154fc35a790bf38cffee7f342f01925a3cebca35c64bcd86f09e7358b3f5bf04</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:968141e2c982370a77eb34e20e397ae5a67780951476b1b3c0c025504182d805</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c3588aa6042eb6992ece7c603b54f491c9c5e4205dc9b4e0b27efb5ae500ec1</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading claims spark plague fears in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc53e1c0f3f43c82fb498c0d53109bd5d1e385730dc5f8b635dcab90043fe6b8</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752--eaca60a52c9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of a lab worker at a plague research institute in Russia has sparked claims about a lab accident, hundreds of infections and international spread. Some of these viral narratives are misleading.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfb1b7d90033ef1e62b90041f7790ec0e333076a82d667a570d879125f1b00ad</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55991989a03c5e76a7d7918094eb1fd4e12946ed886771dc31329a5e51a8062d</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717--5102b97990e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New technology has stopped votes being cast on behalf of dead or absent voters, and turnout has fallen to a record low. But it was a case of deja vu in Bosnia's elections with the same parties winning.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of French schools shut, teen loses hand in protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ebed528f4b866fd0e29aa3d289a8e3b4d6faaecb6b7abbc3ba976690e35382a</id><updated>2026-10-10T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656--d9ec9cc932b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student protests that rocked France last week have prompted authorities to keep up to 500 schools closed on Monday. A teenage boy lost his hand, seemingly while trying to pick up a police tear gas grenade.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
